Describe the metadata of the user's corrected memory statement. The replacement text is authoritative and will be preserved exactly. Reassess its subjects, type, and timing from that text, using the original dated evidence only to resolve references. A correction edits an interpretation; its submission date is not automatically the event date. Relative wording edits the original account: use time_anchor=original. Use correction only when the replacement explicitly establishes a new event relative to submission. Use null when the reference remains ambiguous. Copy time expressions verbatim into facets; the application resolves dates. Use facets.when for an event date and facets.deadline for an explicit completion limit. Return empty temporal fields when the replacement supplies no timing. about identifies the corrected subjects and relationships. Preserve uncertainty.
Use predicate="project_role" for a person’s ongoing role or responsibility in a project; otherwise null. In about, subject identifies whose action or state is described, owner identifies the project whose work is described, and participant identifies another party.
